<template>
    <heading>Loading a project</heading>
    <keywords><li>model</li><li>project loading</li></keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>The root and its ordered child links define the project to load; directory contents do not. This keeps stray or unfinished unlinked files from affecting the model. <code>loadProject()</code> uses the model's privately selected storage object and reads its identically named root article. It follows only ordered child links, rejecting missing files, duplicate links, multiple parents, and cycles. It does not enumerate or load unlinked files.</p><p>A failed load must not leave a mixture of old and new articles. The previous article model is discarded immediately; its replacement and indexes become visible only after complete validation. Failure leaves an empty article model and preserves the selected storage object so the caller can retry. Publishing a complete model also emits <code>ProjectLoaded</code>, so observers can refresh regardless of which caller requested the load. Notification happens only after validation and index construction succeed; selection, partial progress, and failure do not report completion. Loading writes no files and performs no rendering or controller command dispatch. The selecting operation separately reports completion to the HSM.</p><p><code>rootFilename</code> is null while empty or loading. <code>getArticle(filename)</code> returns a record or null; each record contains <code>filename</code>, <code>document</code>, and <code>parentFilename</code> (null for the root). <code>docOrder()</code> traverses the loaded tree, while <code>getBundle(name)</code> and <code>getReferrers(name)</code> provide derived indexes. Returned records are source data; consumers should clone their documents for editing rather than changing them in place and leaving indexes stale. Loading and selection are expected to be serialized by the HSM.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>Model project loading</name>
        <code><![CDATA[async function loadProject() {
    // Discard the old article state before any validation or asynchronous read.
    articles = new Map();
    rootFilename = null;
    bundles = new Map();
    referrers = new Map();

    const project = projectStorage;
    if (!project)
        throw new Error("No project has been selected");
    checkFilename(project.root_filename);
    const loadedArticles = new Map();
    const visiting = new Set();

    async function load(filename, parentFilename) {
        if (visiting.has(filename))
            throw new Error(`Article cycle at '${filename}', linked from '${parentFilename}'`);
        if (loadedArticles.has(filename))
            throw new Error(`Article '${filename}' has more than one parent link`);
        visiting.add(filename);
        let text;
        try {
            text = await project.load(filename);
        } catch (error) {
            throw new Error(`Cannot read '${filename}': ${error.message}`, { cause: error });
        }
        const article = parseArticle(filename, parentFilename, text);
        loadedArticles.set(filename, article);
        for (const child of childFilenames(article))
            await load(child, filename);
        visiting.delete(filename);
    }

    await load(project.root_filename, null);
    const indexes = indexBundles(loadedArticles, project.root_filename);
    articles = loadedArticles;
    bundles = indexes.bundles;
    referrers = indexes.referrers;
    rootFilename = project.root_filename;
    notifications.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent("ProjectLoaded", { detail: { selectionId } }));
}

function getArticle(filename) {
    return articles.get(filename) || null;
}

function* docOrder(filename = rootFilename) {
    const article = articles.get(filename);
    if (!article)
        return;
    yield article;
    for (const child of childFilenames(article))
        yield* docOrder(child);
}

function getBundle(name) {
    return (bundles.get(normalizeBundleName(name)) || []).slice();
}

function getReferrers(name) {
    return [...(referrers.get(normalizeBundleName(name)) || [])];
}
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
